        "decarbonization pathways",
        "model intercomparison study" ;
    DC:abstract "In six scenarios, the RESCUE study shows possible solutions and scope for action for ways to achieve resource-conserving greenhouse gas neutrality in Germany by 2050, analyzing changes in the expansion of renewable energies, levels of effort towards greenhouse gas neutrality, material efficiency and sustainable lifestyles. By 2050, greenhouse gas emissions can be reduced by 95 per cent to 97 per cent compared to 1990. In conjunction with sustainable agricultural and forestry management, net zero emissions can be achieved. The consumption of primary raw materials is reduced by 56 per cent to 70 per cent (although there is also an increase in the use of individual raw materials). This research report provides a detailed overview of the project. Ambitious and rapid action as well as international cooperation are required to implement the transformation pathways described. " ;
    DC:acronym "RESCUE" .

