<http://openenergy-platform.org/ontology/oekg/scenario/2dd771cf-5ee7-6ac2-270c-0b08fa00c300> a OEO:OEO_00000365 ;
    RDFS:label "GreenSupreme" ;
    OEKG:has_full_name "Germany  resource efficient and greenhouse gas neutral  Minimizing future GHG emissions and raw material consumption" ;
    OEKG:scenario_uuid "2dd771cf-5ee7-6ac2-270c-0b08fa00c300" ;
    OEO:OEO_00020220 <http://openenergy-platform.org/ontology/oekg/region/Germany> ;
    OEO:OEO_00020224 "2016",
        "2030",
        "2040",
        "2050" ;
    OEO:has_scenario_descriptor OEO:OEO_00020247,
        OEO:OEO_00020317,
        OEO:OEO_00030009 ;
    DC:abstract "Green Supreme stands for \"Germany - resource efficient and greenhouse gas neutral - Minimizing future GHG emissions and raw material consumption\". The possible change shown here has been characterized from the outset by a pronounced and ambitious joint understanding of the implementation of climate protection and resource conservation, decarbonization and consistent energy saving in Germany and internationally. Quickly integrated, polluter-pays framework conditions set the right incentives across all emission source areas at an early stage. This will achieve a significant reduction in greenhouse gases, particularly in the period up to 2040, and make a fundamental contribution to reducing cumulative emissions and meeting a 1.5 C transformation pathway according to the IPCC." .

