    OEO:has_scenario_descriptor OEO:OEO_00020247,
        OEO:OEO_00020317,
        OEO:OEO_00030009 ;
    DC:abstract """The greenhouse gas reduction scenario (KSG2045) analyzed in this study is based exclusively on the overarching reduction targets of the current Climate Protection Act. The analyses also include digressions, e.g. to be able to classify the robustness of the statements. The ETHOS (Energy Transformation Pathway Optimization Suite) model family, which was developed by the Institute for Techno-Economic Systems Analysis (IEK-3) at Forschungszentrum Jlich, is used for the analysis. This makes it possible to map the energy system on different scales in all its interactions and pathways. The spectrum ranges from detailed regional analyses of possible wind power and PV expansion to spatially resolved energy infrastructure analyses with hourly resolution. In addition, future global energy markets (e.g. synthetic fuels, hydrogen) can be simulated and possible energy imports and exports can be estimated in the context of the transformation process. It is also possible to carry out integrated infrastructure analyses that take all relevant energy sources (electricity, gas, hydrogen, heat) into account simultaneously.

The scenario presented below is a cost-optimal strategy. For this purpose, an energy system model was used that depicts the national energy supply from energy generation to sectoral energy consumption with a high level of detail. The model delivers a strategy at minimum cost, taking into account the exogenously set boundary conditions (e.g. compliance with greenhouse gas reduction targets, meeting energy-related demand). The special feature of the chosen approach, which follows a competitive cost logic, is that all interactions of the energy system are considered simultaneously.""" .

