        OEO:OEO_00020309,
        OEO:OEO_00020312,
        OEO:OEO_00020317,
        OEO:OEO_00030009 ;
    DC:abstract "Carbon-mitigating energy technologies emerge and require strong policy incentives for their uptake and development. The storyline assumes that the effect of grassroots and citizen-led initiatives will be minimal but that strong policy incentives can drive the required engagement of citizens to reach climate targets. This storyline is driven by a strong centralized vision on the part of policymakers and direct partnerships with industry and technology developers who respond to incentives provided by the public sector and provide broad advances in low-carbon energy-related technologies." .

<http://openenergy-platform.org/ontology/oekg/scenario/8c659939-c4c4-b11d-8bbc-0f1549a3c549> a OEO:OEO_00000365 ;
    RDFS:label "dsz-gebaeude" ;
    OEKG:has_full_name "Analysis of Electricity and Heat Demand in Am Ölper Berge District in Lower Saxony" ;
    OEKG:scenario_uuid "8c659939-c4c4-b11d-8bbc-0f1549a3c549" ;
    OEO:OEO_00020222 OEKG:Germany ;
    OEO:OEO_00020224 "2020",
        "2030",
        "2040",
        "2050" ;
    OEO:has_scenario_descriptor OEO:OEO_00020321,
        OEO:OEO_00030010 ;
    DC:abstract """As part of the "Durchstichszenario Gebäude," a flexible building model is being developed to represent various residential building types and integrate them into the co-simulation platform Mosaik. The goal is to comprehensively analyze the thermal and electrical energy demand of a neighborhood. In addition to a reference scenario that reflects the current energy demand, multiple future scenarios are examined, focusing on the gradual integration of renewable energy sources and the reduction of fossil fuel usage. Furthermore, ecological aspects, particularly CO2 emissions, are assessed in detail. The electrification of heat supply, the resulting impacts on the power grid, and the integration of electric vehicle charging are also included in the analysis.
""" .

